	(text "This network interacts with the input \nimpedance of the fuzz stage and \nattenuates the input signal.\nIt affects the amount of guitar volume \nreduction required to prevent saturation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 129.032 160.274 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0553ed01-ed72-465d-a63a-90f9bd8b0e44")
	)
	(text "MIDI IN (MIDI TRS Type A compliant)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 166.116 238.252 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1a3a2d2e-e95e-4398-9c07-fd6df9b1e3b6")
	)
	(text "Rg = 100M returns the gate charge when the JFET switch turns on.\nThe series diode only handles turn-off; it cannot do this.\nDo not omit it: recovery would then depend on diode leakage alone,\nestimated at 23 ms at 25 degC (from 8.7 nA measured at room temperature)\nand about 520 ms at -20 degC (extrapolated).\nLowering it increases pop. Raising it from 100M to 200M reduced pop by\n4.9-6.3 dB (measured); halving it is expected to cost about as much.\nSee ERRATA.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.24 192.544 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "27528e11-fa37-403a-a815-6da16a9a2d32")
	)
	(text "R38: see Rg note below R86."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 284.48 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e238b42a-1afd-5151-b201-1c0f08593749")
	)
	(text "South-West"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 311.658 227.584 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "32e375d1-958a-413a-a54a-d0fc68bd740f")
	)
	(text "The fuzz stage output swings up to about\n5 Vpp (limited by the 5.6 V VCC). The tone\nstage adds up to 5x (+14 dB) of treble\nboost, so peaks can reach the +-8 V rails\nof U4. Use a rail-to-rail output op-amp."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 272.288 149.606 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3ece1dc1-3856-4332-ba3b-b88e28fef07d")
	)
	(text "Q12/Q13 hFE: the built units use\nparts selected to the windows\nmarked between Q12 and Q13\n(measured at I_B = 1.00 uA,\nV_CE = 5 V). The DC operating\npoint (I_C13 = 300 uA,\nI_C12 = 30 uA) is set by the\nR58 feedback. In simulation,\nhFE values of 340-430 change\nI_C13 by less than 0.5% and the\ngain by less than 0.6 dB, mostly\nvia Q13. Other hFE values have\nnot been tested on hardware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.015 66.018 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "40b9f5f4-8dbb-4e3b-bd62-6531350580da")
	)
	(text "Bass(A2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 234.95 135.382 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "41c7e292-cc28-40a1-ae6e-5c7c2047ba07")
	)
	(text "South-East"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 354.838 233.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4889fc6d-c30f-4c78-8c76-87ace2f14aca")
	)
	(text "Using low-leakage capacitors helps reduce switching pop noise.\nFilm capacitors (e.g. PMLCAP) are preferred for C23, C47, and C49 \nover aluminium electrolytic capacitors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 263.144 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "49196345-6dc3-4a12-8a7a-d42b79ddc0b8")
	)
	(text "MIC5205 defines Vref as Vout - Vadj, not as the usual bottom-leg\nreference. R7 22k sits between ADJ and GND; R8 + R9 = 6.2k sits\nbetween OUT and ADJ. Vout = 5.65 V.\nApplying the ordinary divider formula to this gives 1.59 V, which is\nwrong. (Measured VCC is 5.599 V, which reflects the voltage drop across R11.)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 75.438 213.106 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5aa86e31-fcd8-4b44-93a5-5b8f7a1ffd1c")
	)
	(text "Fuzz(B1)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 197.612 149.098 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "63431b29-537d-4d72-b16b-821edd0f36a7")
	)
	(text "These load networks form an LPF with the pickup inductance. \nReducing the guitar volume lowers the Q factor, giving a gentler high-frequency roll-off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.126 17.272 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "658f1a89-8075-4bcc-989d-0a524a089d05")
	)
	(text "R37 and R85 must be the same value. The DC step between bypass and\neffect is dV = Ig * [(R85||R90) - (R37||R90)], so what matters is\nthat they match, not the absolute value. Do not change one without\nthe other. 1% parts are enough: a 2% mismatch adds under 5 uV, far\nbelow the tens of uV measured with matched parts."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 277.114 89.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "65c820de-05a6-4fa2-882f-9994daa406f2")
	)
	(text "R37: see note below."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 284.48 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "466cd59b-eefa-530b-a8c9-af9c40425d25")
	)
	(text "Response(C2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 387.604 205.232 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6c09e38a-940e-49be-a747-c3c3580f5090")
	)
	(text "To minimize pop, the JFET ahead of the\nhigh-gain fuzz stage (Q9) turns on before,\nand turns off after, the effect output\nswitch Q17. The gate RC cells are\nasymmetric on purpose; do not make them\nsymmetric.\nQ4, Q5, Q6, Q9:\n  turn-on (1Meg||220k)*0.1u = 18 ms\n  turn-off 1Meg*0.1u = 100 ms\nQ17 (asymmetric the other way):\n  turn-on (220k+470k)*0.1u = 69 ms\n  turn-off (690k||470k)*0.1u = 28 ms\nSymmetric: Q8 1Meg*0.047u = 47 ms,\nQ10, Q11, Q14, Q15 1Meg*0.1u = 100 ms"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.018 143.826 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6f614328-3e96-4314-8b51-5f46138a742d")
	)
	(text "Vout=5.65V\nVout-Vadj=1.242V\nRbtm=22k\nRtop=6.2k\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 242.824 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "70754c25-769b-4bf5-bf13-978b3bc6cb27")
	)
	(text "I_C13 \n= 300uA(typ.)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.608 117.602 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "71f86e87-aae4-46a3-9c39-9ce5989bfbce")
	)
	(text "hFE as built\nQ12: 365-375\nQ13: 375-385\n(I_B=1.00uA,\nV_CE=5V)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 164.846 124.802 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "baee37f9-400b-54f2-bcde-648d633517cb")
	)
	(text "C35 (100p across R58) adds high-frequency feedback as\na precaution. Removing it made no noticeable change in\nfrequency response or stability on the prototype (no\ndata kept); the high-frequency roll-off is set by C33.\nIf you omit it, check for oscillation at all Fuzz and\nBias settings."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 176.53 168.443 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "875276ce-976c-4171-91b5-7d859aa38409")
	)
	(text "Note the PL9823-F5 pinout. In the datasheet package drawing (leads down),\nthe leads run 4(DIN), 3(VDD), 1(GND), 2(DO) from left to right.\nThe symbol and the standard 4-pin THT LED footprint number them\n4(DIN), 3(VDD), 2(GND), 1(DO): pins 1 and 2 are swapped in number only,\nand the physical order is unchanged.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.954 243.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "88844fdb-f171-49d8-829f-41f65a14dbaf")
	)
	(text "North-East"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 354.838 195.834 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8ef5228a-f522-40b7-8694-96c23ed0da78")
	)
	(text "R90 = 15k and R36 = 3.3k were chosen together. R90 sets the pop\ndip through Ig * (Rd || Rs). Lowering R90 220k -> 15k with\nmatched R37/R85 (100k/220k -> 47k/47k) cut pop by 16.7-19.4 dB;\nR90's own share was not measured. Raising R90 gives some back.\nR36 = 3.3k restores the negative swing lost to the low R90.\nAt 10k, R36 costs bypass THD (0.0286% -> 0.0398%, 1 Vpp, 1 kHz)\nand clipping headroom (11.5 -> about 8 Vpp, 100 Hz). For more low\nend, change C49 to 2.2u instead of raising these resistors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.708 22.352 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9663ce66-7f71-4c47-a177-d37c3805a884")
	)
	(text "R90: see note near R36."
